of the \\(2(n-1)\\) rectangles \\(\\{H_i\\}\\cup\\{V_j\\}\\) covers **all** 1‑entries of \\(M\\).  \n\nThus we have exhibited a covering that uses exactly \\(2n-2\\) tiles.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n#### 4.  Optimality  \n\nEquation (3) shows that no covering can use fewer than \\(2n-2\\) rectangles, while the construction above achieves this number. Hence the minimum possible number of tiles equals \\(2n-2\\).\n\nFor the concrete size \\(n=2025\\),\n\n\\[\n\\min\\#\\text{tiles}=2\\cdot2025-2=4048.\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n#### 5.  Answer  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{4048}\n\\]"
